    "title": "Curved spacetime",
    "pillar": "science",
    "explanation": "Curved spacetime is the idea that gravity comes from the shape of space and time, not from a force pulling at a distance. In this model, mass and energy change the local geometry, and objects move along geodesics — curved paths set by that geometry — so free-falling motion follows the spacetime shape rather than a direct force.\n\nTwo core principles underpin this view. Coordinate independence means physical laws hold in any coordinate system. The equivalence principle says that, locally, the effects of gravity are indistinguishable from acceleration. Together these ideas lead to a geometric description of gravity, formalized by Einstein's field equations.",
